# The labs run in ~/ki-lab, not here. If you work inside this directory
# anyway, these are what the labs generate - tokens, kubeconfigs, keys,
# state. None of it belongs in Git. Model weights live in cluster PVCs,
# never on the laptop.
#
# NOT ignored on purpose: code/infra-proxmox/.terraform.lock.hcl is part
# of the companion code (tofu init for bpg/proxmox 0.116.0).

# Day directories and the exam directory, if you mirror ~/ki-lab here
# (anchored: code/pruefung/ stays tracked)
/tag[0-9][0-9]/
/pruefung/

# Tag 6 - Proxmox API token (~/ki-lab/pve.env)
pve.env
# Tag 8 - RKE2 cluster token (~/ki-lab/rke2-token.env) and kubeconfig
rke2-token.env
rke2.yaml
*.env
.env

# Tag 9 - lab CA exported from the cluster; keys and certificates
lab-ca.crt
*.crt
*.key
*.pem

# Tag 5, 13 - LiteLLM virtual key, OIDC client secret
owui-key.json
oidc-client-secret.txt

# Tag 14 - rendered Tabby config with a LiteLLM key
config.toml

# Tag 15 - S3 credentials for Velero and etcd snapshots; Garage config
s3-backup.cred
*.cred
garage.toml

# Tag 4, 12 - logs and response headers written by the drills
litellm.log
h.txt
hdr.txt

# Tag 7 - OpenTofu: local variables, plans and state (state holds secrets)
terraform.tfvars
*.plan
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Tag 8, 10 - Ansible
*.retry

# Tag 11 - sed -i.bak backup of vllm-chat.yaml
*.bak

# Tag 15 - generated by make_dashboard.py
ki-plattform.json

# Tag 0, 4, 13 - Python venvs and caches (rag_negativ.py imports rag_check)
.venv/
.venv-litellm/
__pycache__/
